        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Labour movement</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">Arose in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/industrial-revolution">Industrial Revolution</a>; spread through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a> and Australasia in the 19th century and across the world in the 20th</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">From about 1800 to the present; outlawed or persecuted in many countries until the later 19th century, and strongest in membership in many industrial countries between the 1940s and the 1970s</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Leading figures</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-owen">Robert Owen</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flora-tristan">Flora Tristan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karl-marx">Karl Marx</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keir-hardie">Keir Hardie</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-gompers">Samuel Gompers</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lech-walesa">Lech Wałęsa</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">Legal trade unions, collective bargaining, the eight-hour day, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/social-insurance">social insurance</a> and labour parties in government; in many countries a decline in membership since the 1980s</span></div>
