    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The labour movement arose with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/industrial-revolution">Industrial Revolution</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, as factory hands, miners and craftsmen combined in trade unions to bargain over wages, hours and conditions.</li><li>Outlawed or harassed in its early decades, it won legal recognition, shorter hours and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/social-insurance">social insurance</a>, and founded parties that governed many countries in the 20th century.</li><li>Its internationals, May Day and the International Labour Organization carried its demands worldwide, and in 1980 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>’s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solidarity-polish-trade-union">Solidarity</a> union challenged communist rule.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The six <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tolpuddle-martyrs">Tolpuddle Martyrs</a>, sentenced in 1834 to transportation to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, were convicted not of forming a union, which was by then legal, but of swearing secret oaths under a law passed after the naval mutinies of 1797.</p></aside>
    </section>

